# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Your private keys go here. This is the safe, not the window.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  WHAT THIS FILE IS
#  A password kept in a safe instead of taped to the window. Your website needs
#  a couple of private passwords to do its job. They can't live in the normal
#  website files, because those files get uploaded and anyone could read them.
#
#  WHAT TO DO
#  1. Make a copy of this file named exactly:  .env.local
#     (Claude can do this for you — say "set up my env file".)
#  2. Paste your keys in below, after each `=` sign. No quotes, no spaces.
#  3. That's it. `.env.local` never gets uploaded anywhere. It is deliberately
#     ignored, so you cannot accidentally publish it.
#
#  ONE THING PEOPLE MISS
#  This file only works on YOUR computer. Your LIVE site needs the same keys
#  entered separately in Vercel (the service that runs your site for the public):
#     Vercel → your project → Settings → Environment Variables
#  Same names, same values. If your forms work on your own machine but not on
#  the live site, this is almost always why.
#
#  NEVER paste these keys into a chat, an email, or site.config.ts. If one ever
#  does get out, delete it in the service that issued it and make a new one —
#  that takes a minute and costs nothing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── GoHighLevel — your contact book and follow-up system ─────────────────────
# When someone fills out a form on your site, this is what lets the site write
# their name into your CRM so you can follow up.
#
# Where to get it: GoHighLevel → Settings → Private Integrations → Create.
# Give it permission to View/Edit Contacts and View/Edit Custom Fields.
#
# Leave this blank and your forms still work perfectly for testing — they just
# record the lead locally instead of sending it. Nothing breaks.
GHL_API_TOKEN=

# (Your GoHighLevel Location ID is NOT secret and does not go here — it goes in
#  site.config.ts under ghl.locationId.)


# ── Anthropic — the chat assistant on your site (optional) ───────────────────
# Powers the little chat window that answers visitor questions. This is a
# company card with your name on it: it's your account, you're billed for it,
# and you can cancel any time.
#
# Where to get it: console.anthropic.com → API Keys.
#
# Leave it blank and the chat window still appears, but it points visitors to
# your phone number and contact form instead of answering. That is a completely
# reasonable way to launch — turn it on later once the site is live.
#
# It costs real money per conversation. Read docs/CHAT-COSTS.md BEFORE you put a
# key here, so the number at the end of the month is one you chose.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
